[20.145972, "o", "R1_ARM=L R1_ENTRY=implementor R1_ROUTES=coordinator=local,implementor=local,verifier=local,plan=local,implement=local,critique=local,smol=local\r\n"]
[219.05253, "o", "import torch\r\nm=XLMRobertaForSequenceClassification.from_pretrained('/app/merged_model')\r\nt=XLMRobertaTokenizer.from_pretrained('/app/merged_model')\r\nm.eval()\r\ni=t('Hola, ¿cómo estás hoy?', return_tensors='pt')\r\nwith torch.no_grad(): l=m(**i).logits\r\nprint('reload ok, num_labels:', m.config.num_labels, 'argmax:', int(l.argmax()))\r\n\" 2>&1 | grep -vE \"Warning|Loading\" — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash cd /app && python3 -c \" from transformers import XLMRobertaForSequence…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.8-27b — 16 tool call(s) so far\r\n  qwen3.8-27b — 17 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ todo \r\n    ✓ todo — 6/6 done\r\nAll done. Summary:\r\n\r\n**Setup** (scripts at `/app/setup_model.py` and `/app/detect.py`):\r\n- Installed CPU torch 2.15, transformers 5.22, peft 0.21.\r\n- Downloaded `FacebookAI/xlm-roberta-base` → `/app/model_cache/xlm-roberta-base` and the LoRA adapter → `/app/model_cache/xlm-roberta-base-lora-language-detection`.\r\n- Built `XLMRobertaForSequenceClassification` from the base weights with `num_labels"]
[219.052652, "o", "=20` and saved it (with tokenizer) to `/app/model_cache/xlm-roberta-base`.\r\n- Applied the adapter via `PeftModel` (LoRA r=8 on query/value + the 20-class `classifier` from `modules_to_save`), then `merge_and_unload()` and saved the merged model + tokenizer to `/app/merged_model/`. Both configs now report 20 labels.\r\n\r\n**Detection results** (`/app/detection_results.json`, argmax of logits, no class-ID knowledge used):\r\n\r\n| text | class | confidence |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Bonjour… | 6 | 0.9753 |\r\n| Hola… | 5 | 0.9890 |\r\n| Guten Tag… | 2 | 0.9973 |\r\n| Ciao… | 8 | 0.9888 |\r\n| Olá… | 12 | 0.9896 |\r\n| Привет… | 13 | 0.9856 |\r\n| こんにちは… | 9 | 0.9649 |\r\n| 你好… | 19 | 0.9360 |\r\n| مرحبا… | 0 | 0.9880 |\r\n| Hello… | 4 | 0.9737 |\r\n\r\nAll 10 predictions are distinct, high-confidence, and consistent with the adapter's 20-language label set (ar, bg, de, el, en, es, fr, hi, it, ja, nl, pl, pt, ru, sw, th, tr, ur, vi, zh). Verified by reloading the merged model from disk and re-running a"]
[219.052666, "o", " sample — it loads cleanly and reproduces the same argmax.\r\n\r\n[result] role=implementor model=qwen3.8-27b tools=17 surface=1ff9b2b7005d\r\n"]
